Pass snooze()'s 64-bit argument correctly in osyield, fixing the startup hang.

snooze() takes a bigtime_t (int64) of microseconds. Under the 32-bit cdecl
ABI that is two stack words, but osyield called it through sysvicall1, which
pushes a single word. The high half of the argument was therefore whatever
the stack happened to contain: when it was non-zero, this yield slept for
(garbage << 32) microseconds, which is indistinguishable from forever.

lock2 calls osyield() during its spin phase while holding m.locks and a P,
so the thread froze inside libc still holding the P. Nothing else could be
scheduled: runnable goroutines sat queued, idle Ms sat unused, and the CPU
was idle because the thread really was asleep. It looked random because it
depended on stack garbage, and it was rare at GOMAXPROCS=1 because with
little contention lock2 seldom reaches the spin phase. The asm osyield1
already pushed a proper 64-bit zero, which is why only this path broke.

Measured with haiku32/testdata/stress/lockstress.go, alternating builds
run-for-run: 0 hangs in 20 with this fix, 12 in 20 without. tailscaled's
LocalAPI then came up 6 times out of 6, each in 1s, where it used to wedge
roughly one start in seven.

--- a/src/runtime/os2_haiku.go
+++ b/src/runtime/os2_haiku.go
@@ -651,7 +651,19 @@
 
 //go:nosplit
 func osyield() {
-	sysvicall1(&libc_snooze, 0)
+	// snooze() takes a 64-bit bigtime_t. In the 32-bit cdecl ABI that is TWO
+	// stack words, so it must be passed with sysvicall2; sysvicall1 pushes only
+	// the low word and leaves the high word as whatever the stack happened to
+	// hold. When that garbage was non-zero, this "yield" slept for
+	// (garbage << 32) microseconds - effectively forever.
+	//
+	// That was the Haiku/386 startup hang. lock2 calls osyield() in its spin
+	// phase while holding m.locks and a P, so the m froze inside libc holding
+	// the P, with the CPU idle and idle Ms sitting unused, and nothing else
+	// could be scheduled. It looked random because it depended on stack
+	// garbage, and it was rare at GOMAXPROCS=1 because with little contention
+	// lock2 seldom reaches the spin phase.
+	sysvicall2(&libc_snooze, 0, 0)
 }
 
 func area_for(addr uintptr) {
